\f3 \cf6 \cb7 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Creates single-UMI consensus reads and calls somatic variants.\
Starts with an unmapped BAM file with the UMI in a tag (`RX` by default).
\f1 \cf0 \cb1 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \

\f3 \cf6 \cb7 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The reads are aligned with bwa-mem, then duplicate marked using the UMI tag, grouped by molecular ID to create a "grouped" BAM file, and consensus called to produce per-molecule consensus reads. The consensus reads are aligned with bwa-mem and subsequently filtered.
\f1 \cf0 \cb1 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
1. 
\f0\b Add UMI information to bam file
\f1\b0 \
	UMI-tag is added as tag RX:NNNNNNNNN\
	if UMI needs to be added from fastq to mapped bam not containing RX tag, use\
$ fgbio AnnotateBamWithUmis -Xms500m -Xmx10g -i input.bam -f index.fastq.gz -o output.bam\
	!!! Xmx has to be set pretty high as the entire index.fastq is loaded into memory \'97> adjust cores accordingly!\
\

\f0\b 2. Group reads by UMI
\f1\b0 \
	reads are sorted by template, mapping position and then by UMI-sequence\
	input bams have to contain mate-mapping-quality tag (MQ)\
[[	- if you find reads without MQ-tag or missing mate:\
		$ 
\f0\b picard FixMateInformation
\f1\b0  I=input.bam O=output.bam\
			sorts by query and fixes mate information\
	or\
		$ sambamba sort -n -t threads -m max_mem -l compression_level -i input.bam -o output1.bam\
			sorts by query name\
		$ 
\f0\b \cf8 \CocoaLigature0 fgbio SetMateInformation
\f1\b0  -i output1.bam -x -o output2.bam\
			sets the proper MQ tag that is missing in many reads\
			options: -x		ignore unmapped reads (should not be there but are!)\
]]\
\
\
	once your bam file has set the proper tags, you can run the UMI-grouping:\
	$ 
\f0\b fgbio GroupReadsByUmi
\f1\b0  -i input.bam -o output.bam -s adjacency\
		options: 	-m 20			set the minimum mapping quality\
				-s			sets the strategy for grouping \'97> adjacency is best\
				--edits 1		for targeted-sequencing data, this value can be put higher\
\
\cf0 \CocoaLigature1 	Tags:\
		MI:Z					unique UMI-ID for the UMI-group ID\cf8 \CocoaLigature0 \
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b 3. Call consensus reads
\f1\b0 \
	reads of the same UMI-group are collapsed into a consensus read\
	bam has to be processed with GroupReadsByUmi tool\
\
	$ 
\f0\b fgbio -Xmx2g CallMolecularConsensusReads
\f1\b0  -i input.umi-grouped.bam -o ouput.consensus.bam\
		--min-reads=1			minimum number of observations\
	options:\
		--error-rate-pre-umi=45\
		--error-rate-post-umi=40		set to 30\
		--min-input-base-quality=10	\
		--output-per-base-tags=true	set to false to save data (needs to be included for per-base-filtering)\
		--rejects=rejects.bam		file to save rejected reads to\
\

\f0\b 4. Filter consensus reads
\f1\b0 \
	$ 
\f0\b fgbio FilterConsensusReads
\f1\b0  -i input.consensus.bam -o output.filtered.bam \
		-M 1 						min reads supporting a consensus\
		-N 20						min base quality\
		-r hg38.fa					ref genome\
		--max-read-error-rate=0.025	-E	max raw-read error rate across consensus read		--max-base-error-rate=0.1		-e	max error rate for single base	\
	options: 	\
		-N=40						min base-quality for call\
		-q						min mean-base-quality across consensus read\
		--max-no-call-fraction		-n	max fraction of no-calls in the filtered read\
\
	(IDT:	-E 0.05 -N 40 -e 0.1 -n 0.1)\
\

\f0\b 5. remap consensus reads to genome
\f1\b0 \
	$ picard SamToFastq\
		I=output.filtered.bam\
		F=/dev/stdout\
		INTERLEAVE=true |\
	  bwa mem -p -M -t \{threads\} hg38.fa /dev/stdin |\
	  picard MergeBamAlignment\
		UNMAPPED=output.filtered.bam\
		ALIGNED=/dev/stdin\
		O=output.filter_mapped.bam\
		R=hg38.fa\
		SO=coordinate\
		ALIGNER_PROPER_PAIR_FLAGS=true\
		MAX_GAPS=-1\
		ORIENTATIONS=FR\
		VALIDATION_STRINGENCY=SILENT\
		CREATE_INDEX=true\
		ADD_MATE_CIGAR=true\
		CLIP_OVERLAP= ???}